Fant basically took this idea of incompleteness and turned it into an architectural principle.

03:05.420 --> 03:10.040
See, unlike traditional computer circuits that rely on external clocks to time everything.

03:10.240 --> 03:14.360
Making the engineer responsible for making sure inputs are ready at just the right microsecond.

03:14.700 --> 03:20.640
Precisely. Which is a huge burden. NCL circuits, they internalize this completeness check.

03:20.640 --> 03:26.340
So, wait, instead of an external clock forcing order, the circuit itself becomes aware of when

03:26.340 --> 03:27.560
its inputs are actually ready.

03:27.720 --> 03:33.400
Exactly. NCL gates are fundamentally different. They only assert a valid result, a true or a false

