if, and only if, all their inputs are valid data.

03:37.360 --> 03:38.100
And if not.

03:38.200 --> 03:45.420
If any input is still in an unknown or not ready state, NCL calls this an NL state, the gate simply

03:45.420 --> 03:47.540
outputs NL. It just...

03:47.540 --> 03:47.980
It waits.

03:47.980 --> 03:53.540
It waits. This strict discipline means no gate can ever produce data from incomplete or

03:53.540 --> 03:59.820
uncertain inputs. The circuit literally self-regulates. It cycles between an all NL state, signaling

03:59.820 --> 04:03.940
it's cleared and ready for new information, and then a data resolution state where the

04:03.940 --> 04:04.820
processing happens.

04:04.900 --> 04:07.800
So, it's delay insensitive. It doesn't need that global clock.

04:07.900 --> 04:11.380
Yeah. That's the key. It doesn't need it. It waits until its inputs are complete. It

04:11.380 --> 04:12.560
internalizes the timing.

